#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2351 expect=noViolation domain=SE
#note "PLAN-join-key-one-side-absent-drop QK18 (3) (owner 2026-10-11): DS without USUBJID does NOT reach the QK16 ERROR for FDA-SE2351 - the Check's leading `USUBJID in $ds_usubjid` reads distinct(USUBJID, domain=\"DS\"), which holds no subject when DS lacks the column, so the conjunct is false on every record and the grouped DS extreme (group=[USUBJID]) is never read. Pinned as the measured answer: silent, no ERROR. Why it is data-dependent here (owner QK19, 2026-10-11): FDA-SE2351 has a rule-level Grouping, whose path has no absent-column fold reading the bindings up front, so the lazy grouped binding is read only behind the and short-circuit (E2) - the same Check without the Grouping ERRORs on this shape (measured on FDA-SE2270). A gate declaring DS.USUBJID would turn it into a SKIP."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 3 | FUP  | Follow-up | 2020-01-21 | 2020-01-25
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | TRT  | Treatment | 2020-01-05 | 2020-01-20
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN | Screening | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-04
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 1 | MOVED TO RECOVERY  | RECOVERY           | 2020-01-05
S1 | DS | 2 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-01-20

